roval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node blue and hot  left axilla  is a single 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  short suture superior  long suture lateral  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibrofatty tissue  with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior orange  lateral green and medial yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm poorly defined stellate firm mass with adjacent hemorrhage and fibrosis  the latter consistent with biopsy site  Extending away from this region is an arm of firm fibrous tissue which abuts the lateral margin  The stellate region is 1 3cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the anterior margin  greater than 2cm from the superior margin  1 8cm from the inferior margin and 0 6cm from the medial margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  no block E   B  Mass to closest anterior and posterior margin C  Fibrous arm approaching lateral margin D  Closest medial margin F  Mass G  Superior margin en face H  Inferior margin en face V  Mass Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  final shaved medial margin  are four fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring 7 x 3 x 1cm in aggregate submitted in cassettes I P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved lateral margin  is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring 5 x 3 x 1 3cm  