Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 12 CLINICAL DATA  57 y o  female with h o invasive lobular carcinoma of the left breast                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY EDGE   SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  THESE SLIDES WERE REVIEWED BY DR  A  ZEMBOWICZ  WHO CONCURS WITH THE DIAGNOSIS  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 40                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm unoriented simple mastectomy specimen  Attached is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin ellipse  with a areola measuring 3 0cm in diameter and a nipple measuring 1 5cm in diameter  The skin ellipse is eccentrically located on the roughly ovoid mastectomy specimen  and to provide a frame of reference the side containing the skin ellipse will be arbitrarily designated  inferior  and the opposite side will be arbitrarily designated  superior   The skin ellipse is remarkable for a 2 4cm curvilinear  well healed scar along its inferior edge centrally  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm semilunar firm to hard lesion at the superior border of the ellipse  Otherwise  it is tan and unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  The external surface of the breast parenchyma is also unremarkable  The deep  posterior  margin is inked black and the anterior margin is inked blue  The tissue is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm biopsy cavity  filled with a viscous brown fluid  located subjacent to the scar noted on the skin ellipse  At its closest approach  the biopsy cavity extends to within 0 5cm of the deep margin and to within 0 6cm of the anterior margin  Surrounding the biopsy cavity is abundant firm white scar tissue which is focally yellow and gritty  These ill defined foci of yellow gritty material extend to and abut the deep margin  spanning a region measuring 2 2cm  Elsewhere  the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The tissue is extensively searched for lymph nodes  but none is identified  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity to closest deep margin B E  remaining biopsy cavity with surrounding yellow gritty scar tissue F G  scar tissue adjacent to biopsy cavity H  breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavity I  red lesion at superior border of skin ellipse Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  axillary nodes  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 8cm in greatest dimension  They are submitted as cassettes J O  with cassette O containing a single lymph node sectioned  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  mastectomy margin skin edge  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse with a small amount of yellow fatty subcutis attached  excised to a depth of 0 6cm centrally  The skin is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nonpigmented  round  raised  well circumscribed lesion  No other lesions are identified  The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely as cassettes P R  with the raised lesion in cassette R  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  David Nathan H