a follicular pattern  The B cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and bcl 2  Follicles are delineated by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  staining  With antibody to T lineage associated antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of many small cells in the interfollcular region  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  The slides from the prior lymph node biopsy have been reviewed   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The findings are similar to those in the current case  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 33     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     With antibody to bcl 6 on a section from the axillary nodes  many of the atypical lymphoid cells are stained  This provides additional support for the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE grams  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and an anterior tan white skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm  with an unremarkable nipple and a 2 5cm well healed linear scar in the lateral portion of the skin  The specimen is inked in black posteriorly and blue anteriorly  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white stellate  vaguely nodular firm mass  with focal areas of calcification and fat necrosis  The tumor mass is present