 of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibrofatty tissue with a short stitch marking the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The anterior surface is inked black and the deep  posterior  surface is inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from lateral to medial in A through J  Another specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  and consists of three fibrofatty tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm in aggregate  One of these fragments has a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm very firm  white  fibrous  ill defined nodule  This nodule is fully submitted in K and L  The second fragment also has a firm  white fibrous area measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is somewhat stellate shaped  Fully submitted in M and N  The last fragment appears to be purely adipose tissue and is fully submitted in O  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                