te near large mass where the two metal coils were identified   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Small mass entirely submitted with posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable tissue superior to small mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable tissue inferior to large mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional tissue inferior to small mass  Unfixed  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVED_DATE  left axillary sentinel node   is a 4 x 4 x 1cm piece of unremarkable yellow  lobulated  firm tissue  The firm areas are entirely frozen as FX  1 to FX 1D and submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVED_DATE  left breast lateral margin    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of adipose tissue and tan white fibrous tissue with a suture designating the new margin  which is inked  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVED_DATE  left breast posterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of adipose tissue and tan white fibrous tissue  which is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 TO  1D   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 23 58PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor prote