atory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 0 6cm fragment of breast tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibroadipose cut surface with focally hemorrhagic areas  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm nodule which corresponds to the microcalcification on mammogram  The suspicious nodule is submitted in cassette A  and the remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes B through H  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS   FIRM LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
