 value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 23 x 16 x 6 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying 22 x 10 5cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  and a 6 0cm linear scar located in the lateral upper quadrant  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail is also attached to the specimen  The anterior superior surface is inked blue  the anterior inferior surface is inked green  and the deep resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm cavity filled with brown red hematoma surrounded by indurated  fibrotic parenchyma  abutting the closest deep resection margin  and 2 5cm from the closest anterior superior and 2 5cm from the closest anterior inferior resection margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Section code  A  biopsy cavity and adjacent closest deep resection margin  B F  representative sections of the indurated wall of the biopsy cavity  G I  representative sections of the breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity  J N  representative sections of the axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ag