HOT SPOT  O  CT 295    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRA NODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  0  CT  186    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  0  CT  585    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPHADENECTOMY  LEVEL I    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 5 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 95 at 16 46                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY