ponsible provider processing was deemed to be in the best interest of patient care  in accordance with Hospital policy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm excision specimen with a needle localization wire in place  and accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is inked entirely black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm well defined  tan white firm mass  which is focally abutting the black inked margin  The remainder of the specimen is remarkable for a scant amount of tan gray fibrous tissue and yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue fragment  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal tan gray fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass submitted in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section away from mass  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node  which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 7 additional containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Higgins  REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  anterior margin  left breast   are 2 portions of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with black stitches along 1 aspect  which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The stitched aspects are inked black  and the fragments are serially sectioned to reveal focally dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The former is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the latter as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  deep posterior margin  left breast   are 2 portions of tan red fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  which measure REMOVED_D