d and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a 25 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm mastectomy specimen with an attached 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm axillary tail and a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple bearing skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm ill defined  stellate tan mass  which comes to 0 3cm from the posterior resection margin  2 5cm from the anterio superior resection margin and 5cm from anterior resection margin  and is far away from the inferior  lateral  and medial resection margins  A 0 3cm tan white nodule is identified 0 3cm from the tumor which comes to 2cm from the anterio superior resection margin  Also identified adjacent to the tumor is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan firm nodule  which comes to 2 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin  A 3cm area of hemorrhage is present 10cm lateral to the tumor  In the axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  are identified  SECTION CODE A  Tumor with posterior resection margin B  Tumor with anterio superior resection margin C E  Additional section of tumor  with deep margin in D F  0 3cm nodule G  0 6cm nodule H  Hemorrhagic area I L  Lymph nodes  the largest 6 lymph nodes are bivalved and submitted in I K  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO