ocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan white irregular  rubbery fibrofatty tissue  with a stitch designating the new margin  inked black   The opposing surface is red yellow and chalky  The cut surface reveals focal yellow chalky areas surrounding the previous biopsy site  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with a history of right breast cancer diagnosed by core biopsy at an outside hospital  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH DENSE STROMAL SCLEROSIS  B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES  2 11   SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  11 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2 Extracapsular extension  Marked Other forms of axillary involvement  Soft tissue metastasis  Note  Sections of the lymph nodes reveal metastatic carcinoma growing in broad sheets and trabeculae with geographic zones of necrosis  The tumor nearly replaces the largest lymph node and is also noted in the adjacent soft tissue  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with focal areas of squamous differentiation  The tumor cells have abundant dense cytoplasm and enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with irregular contours  coarse vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  Numerous mitotic figures  including atypical mitoses  are readily identified with a mitotic figure count of 22 mitotic figures in 10 high powered fields  The morphologic findings are compatible with the patient s reported history of metastatic poorly differentiated carcinoma of the breast  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification are pending on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   are 2 fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue that measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Each fragment is inked black  The largest fragment is serially sectioned to reveal a white firm cut surface with no distinct mass or lesion grossly appreciated  The first fragment is serially sectioned from one end to the other to reveal firm white tissue with no masses or lesions grossly appreciated  The entire specimens are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire large fragment sequentially submitted from one end to the other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire smaller fragment  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary nodes   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue that aggregate to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  Multiple candidate lymph nodes are identified ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibroadipose tissue with possible candidate lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 55 35PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Right Axilla  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 38 14PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Lymph Node  Right Axilla  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  961  to chromosome 17 signals  102  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 32 54PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Excision PART B  Lymph Nodes  Right Axilla   Dissection  report_end  , Unchecked.
