Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA  54 year old female  status post lesion on mammogram  Fine needle aspiration is positive for infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  APPROACHING TO WITHIN 1 MM OF THE SUPERIOR INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension  The surgical resection margins of the main specimen are close  superior   0 1cm   but negative  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified     LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENT   EXCISION  SEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA  0 7   SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA  0 1   SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL AND SUPERIOR TISSUE   EXCISION  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  MEDIAL RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  LENTIGO  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 09                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  LUMPECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   5   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 05     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  pa