GIN  UNORIENTED   EXCISION  FOCAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  ASSOCIATED WITH MINUTE FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVOLVING 2 OF 4 BLOCKS  SPANNING UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The inferior margin is inked black  the superior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm indurated gray white poorly delineated region which abuts the inferior margin and comes to 0 4cm of the superior  0 4cm of the anterior  0 6cm of the lateral  1 0cm of the medial  and 1 1cm of the anterior margin  A silver metal clip is noted along the anterior aspect of the area  and the area is between the two localization wires  The remaining mammary tissue is dense gray white and fibrous  Representative sections are submitted from posterior to anterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the tissue bearing the silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the firm area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  posterior right margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unoriented tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  The unoriented specimen is serially secti