atory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in five parts  Labeled  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with a suture indicating superior margin of the specimen  At the center of the specimen is a 2 5cm x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm grossly unremarkable portion of nipple and areola  Also present superior to the nipple and areola is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central 1 7cm long scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal no definite biopsy cavity underlying the surface scar  The remaining breast parenchyma ranges in color from tan to yellow  and is largely fibrotic with focal cystic change  Section code  A D scar and underlying tissue entirely E H further representative portions of breast Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level 1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of yellow tan lobulated fibrofatty tissue  which is dissected to reveal six tan to dark brown lymph nodes ranging in size up to 1 5cm  and measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in aggregate  Section code  I K two lymph nodes each  all bisected Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level 2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of yellow tan fibrofatty tissue containing two brown rubbery lymph nodes measuring up to 0 8cm  and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The lymph nodes are bisected and submitted entirely in L  Labeled  left axilla  hot spot  1  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of yellow tan fibrofatty tissue containing a tan  rubbery lymph  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node  Bisected and submitted entirely in M  Labeled  left axilla  hot spot  1  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of yellow tan fibrofatty tissue  containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan  rubbery lymph node  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in N  Gross Description by  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Thomas L Toth  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  BREAST AXILARY  LEVEL 1  PART C  BREAST AXILLARY  LEVEL 2  PART D  LEFT AXILLARY  HOT SPOT 1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PART E  LEFT AXILLARY  HOT SPOT 1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    report_end  , Unchecked.
