anging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension are identified in the axillary portion of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node  Gross Dictation by Julia Turbiner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 48 CLINICAL DATA  Advanced breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90    MODERATELY AND POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 AND REMOVED_DATE  ULCERATED WITH FOCAL PAGETOID SPREAD AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   10    SEE NOTE  2  FOUR OUT OF FOUR LYMPH NODES POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  A focus of infiltrating carcinoma is present within less than 0 05cm at an inferior deep radial surgical resection margin  The other examined margins on the main specimen are free of carcinoma  Lymphatic vascular invasion is present  In the axillary tail  four recognizable lymph nodes are positive for carcinoma  but multiple nodules of tumor are present at this localization  some of which may represent totally replaced lymph nodes with soft tissue extension  Multiple satellite nodules of tumor are also present within the breast parenchyma  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN  BIOPSY  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF HIGHLY ATYPICAL CELLS SUGGESTIVE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  This focus is not present in deeper permanent section  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR SKIN MARGIN  BIOPSY  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  LEFT NEW SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN  2  RESECTION  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  LEFT NEWEST SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN  3   RESECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 25                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 28 x 10 8cm ellipse of white skin containing a 2 7cm in diameter distorted nipple and areola  The surrounding 7 x 6cm skin is firm  darkened and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm ulceration inferomedially and a 3 3cm linear indentation   scar   lateral to the nipple  The fibroadipose tissue deep to the skin measures 24 x 17 x 8 5cm and is contiguous with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  Deep to the firm area on the skin is an 8 x 7 x 5cm tan to white  firm  ill defined mass  Strands of tan tissue approach to within 0 5cm of the superior and inferior superficial soft tissue margins  Multiple REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm satellite nodules are present in the specimen and one 0 4cm tan nodule abuts the inferior deep inked margin  However  the medial and lateral resectiion margins are greater than 2cm from gross tumor  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  All the lymph nodes are white and rubbery  Section Code A B   nipple and tumor C D   representative ulcer E F   firm skin adjacent to nipple G   scar H K   representative tumor L M   superior superficial margin  radial sections N   inferior superficial  radial margin O   medial  en face margin P   lateral  en face margin Q   deep radial margin R U   lymph nodes EE FF   deep margin  radial section GG   deep inferior margin  radial section Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are multiple parts  Labeled  superior margin left breast  is a tissue fragment  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  soft  yellow tan  submitted entirely as frozen  1 in V  Labeled  inferior margin left breast  is a fragment of soft  yellow tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  entirely frozen as frozen  2 and submitted in W  Labeled  new superior margin  is a 16cm long and 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm  A stitch designates the opposite surface to the new superior margin  The new margin is inked and representative  non stitch  margin is frozen as frozen  3  5  in X to Z respectively  Additional unfrozen new superior margin from the peripheral ends of the skin ellipse are submitted in AA and BB  Labeled  superior margin  3  left breast  and  suture on inferior margin  is a 7 x 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm with a suture in place on the inferior margin  The skin ellipse is unremarkable  Representative new superior margin is taken from the central portion of the ellipse and frozen as frozen  6 in CC  The remainder of this newest superior margin is entirely submitted in DD  Gross Description by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Resident  William H  Yong  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LEFT BREAST SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN   SMALL FOCUS OF ATYPICAL CELLS SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC OF CARCINOMA  AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  EXPLAINED TO SURGEON   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LEFT BREAST INFERIOR MARGIN   CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FSDX REMOVED_DATE  NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN   2   MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF CARCINOMA  CENTER SECTION  FSDX 6  NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN   3   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  JACKSON OPERATING ROOM REPORTS TO   Unknown  PART A  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN  BIOPSY  PART B  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR SKIN MARGIN  BIOPSY  PART C  BREAST  LEFT NEW SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN  BIOPSY  PART D  BREAST  LEFT NEW SUPERIOR SKIN MARGIN 3  PART E  BREAST LEFT  MASTECTOMY    report_end  , Unchecked.
