ne binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached localizing wire and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm white nodule  grossly extending to multiple inked margins  A representative section of the nodule is frozen and saved frozen  The remainder of the nodular area is submitted entirely in cassettes A F  Representative sections of the remaining grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma submitted in cassettes G J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David Bent Smith  M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
