ite including overlying skin  G H  nipple with adjacent fibrous breast tissue  I  biopsy site  J  fibrous area 3cm lateral to biopsy site  K L  representative sections of unremarkable breast  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Abdominal fat  are four segments of tan pink unremarkable skin with associated tan yellow subcutaneous tissue  The largest to smallest respectively  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Two segments of tan white unremarkable fibrofatty tissue are also submitted  10 x 3 x 2cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm  respectively  Section Code  M P  representative sections of skin and subcutaneous tissue  Q R  representative sections of fibrofatty tissue  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Martha Elizabeth Meaney  M D  PART A  BREAST TISSUE  RIGHT  PART B  ABDOMINAL FAT   report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA  2mm carcinoma with questionable margins excised at outside institution                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH NEUROENDOCRINE FEATURES   REMOVED_DATE CM  SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC FOR INVASION  PRESENT AT THE RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  SCANT  3  FIBROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HISTIOCYTES AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  SPECIMEN ENTIRELY SUBMITTED  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  The tumor is present at the margin designated by the short suture  Focal cells are positive for a PAS and a grimelius stain  the positive grimelius stain confirms focal neuroendocrine differentiation  Immunohistochemical studies for chromogranin and for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor proteins will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 27     SPECIAL STAINS Addendum     THE CARCINOMA CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR CHROMOGRANIN WITH IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINING    Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number are three parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a 18 gram fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm with central healing scar 2 0cm in length  There is a long suture at one end of the specimen and a short suture at a side of the specimen  the long suture is designated 12 o clock  and the short suture designated 9 o clock  The external surface of the specimen is unremarkable  lobulated  yellow pink fibroadipose tissue with focal cautery artifact and fibrous tissue  The external surface is inked black with the 9 o clock aspect inked yellow on black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central biopsy cavity REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm surrounded by gritty  bright yellow  granular tissue and fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through K with the 12 o clock end in A and the 6 o clock end in K  Labeled  left axillary contents  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm containing several nodules  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette L through R  Labeled  left axillary nodes  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue containing a central lymph node REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The largest is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette S  the smaller three are submitted entirely in cassette T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION PART B  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS  EXCISION , Unchecked.
