vity is firm and red yellow mottled in color  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of adipose tissue with dense fibrous bands dissecting through it  Several lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in greatest dimension with a pink tan homogeneous cut surface  Section Code  A  nipple  B  scar  C H  biopsy cavity  I  skin and biopsy cavity  J  random sections from breast  K L M  lymph nodes  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  Frank J Leonard vidal  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 32 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right breast needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   FOCALLY EXTENDING TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES AND LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FROM MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   2   SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  LOW GRADE   PREDOMINANTLY CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS WITH SEVERAL FOCI EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE  3  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Definite blood vessel or lymphatic invasion is not identified  ER and PR will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm stellate  white  firm mass abutting the inked surface  A representative section of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  with representative sections of the rest of the remaining tissue are in D through J  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
