 REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm strand of breast tissue which also crosses the exposed aspect of the biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is lined by red brown granulation tissue  fat necrosis  and focal fibrous areas  No areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma are identified  The margins are as follows  Posterior biopsy cavity exposed Anterior 0 4cm Superior 0 5cm Inferior  medial and lateral   4 0cm  Section code  A  biopsy cavity with posterior margin B  biopsy cavity with anterior margin C D  biopsy cavity E G  representative parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary fat ranging in size from 0 3cm up to 1 6cm  A representative section of each is submitted in H J  A second specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast reduction  is a 120gm  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  aggregate of multiple fragments of breast tissue  Two fragments of tissue have overlying skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE each  No discrete lesions are identified  Along with the specimen is a 13 x 3 5cm thin fragment of irregular shaped unremarkable skin without subcutaneous tissue  Representative sections are submitted in cassette K T  Resident  WEN JING  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MAMMOPLASTY   report_end  , Unchecked.
