 situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of the ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL  SUPERIOR TO LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  RARE ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS PRESENT IN 1 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  4 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan yellow fibrofatty breast excision specimen  There is a short stitch designating superior and a long lateral  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  On sectioning  three separate masses are identified  The largest superior mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm and is ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  coming to 0 4cm from the posterior  1 0cm from the medial  1 2cm from the superior  1 4cm from the anterior  1 6cm from the lateral  and 3 1cm from the inferior margins  Located 1 5cm inferior is another ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  indurated mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  This mass is 0 5cm from the posterior  0 8cm from the medial  1 2cm from both the anterior and the lateral  1 0cm from the inferior and 4 6cm from the superior margins  The third indurated  ill defined mass is located at the anterolateral aspect  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  It is 0 5cm from the anterior  0 6cm from the lateral  0 8cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the superior  2 8cm from the medial  and 4 5cm from the inferior margins  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consists of tan white fibrotic tissue and yellow  focally hemorrhagic and lobulated fat  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire superior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire inferior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire anterolateral mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening parenchyma between the superior and the inferior mass with the aspect closest to the superior mass inked orange  not a margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lymph node  suspicious    are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in aggregate of yellow  lobulated fat which contains four potential lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Rebecca J DiIorio  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s ac